  "labeling_note": "Only the four Stopping reference cases are relabeled here. Each is Compliant under the frozen synthetic public-highway, properly authorized sign and through-highway assumptions: measured zero velocity before the applicable reference, followed by waiting for the initial through vehicle to clear. The further vehicle remains outside the intersection during the subject crossing. Its programmed braking is not, by itself, evidence that the subject yielded; the annotation also checks measured separation and a constant-current-speed arrival projection throughout the crossing. This projection is explanatory evidence, not a statutory numerical immediate-hazard threshold. For case 4, the review judgment treats the last safe approach boundary, with the vehicle front approximately 0.044 m upstream and sampled modeled visibility of at least 200 m on the incoming approaches, as the nearest practical stopping point with a view. This is an explicit scenario judgment; the source geometry identifies a candidate and does not independently establish a legal nearest point or human perception. Original automated inconclusive assessments remain in review_label_history. The other comparisons are unchanged.",
